ents is the subject of a critical examination in a recent paper by Cowley <jats:italic>et al<\/jats:italic>. (1977). The effective temperature of the star is about 6100 K (Przybylski, 1977) which is substantially lower than the temperature of any known Ap star. However, the effective temperature of HD 101065 is still subject to controversy (Wegner, 1976).<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/s1323358000015137","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2016,7,27]],"date-time":"2016-07-27T08:56:02Z","timestamp":1469609762000},"page":"143-144","update-policy":"http:\/\/dx.doi.org\/10.1017\/policypage","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Search for Light Variations of HD 101065"],"prefix":"10.1017","volume":"3","author":[{"given":"A.","family":"Przybylski","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"56","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2016,4,25]]},"reference":[{"key":"S1323358000015137_ref6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/mnras\/177.1.99"},{"key":"S1323358000015137_ref3","first-page":"225","volume":"15","author":"Przybylski","year":"1967","journal-title":"Postepy Astronomii"},{"key":"S1323358000015137_ref7","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1086\/129908"},{"key":"S1323358000015137_ref1","unstructured":"Cowley Ch. R. , Cowley Anne P. , Aikman G. Ch. and Crosswhite Hannah M. , Astrophys. J. (in press) (1977)."},{"key":"S1323358000015137_ref5","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/mnras\/110.4.395"},{"key":"S1323358000015137_ref4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/mnras\/178.4.735"},{"key":"S1323358000015137_ref2","first-page":"31","volume":"10","author":"Jarzebowski","year":"1960","journal-title":"Acta. Astron"}],"container-title":["Publications of the Astronomical Society of Australia"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/services\/aop-cambridge-core\/content\/view\/S1323358000015137","content-type":"unspecified","content-v